Sung Song (sysong@husc8.harvard.edu) wrote:
: 1) Is there any way to avoid the paralysis of a gelatinous cube? (like a
: paralysis resistance intrinsic? I had sleep restistance BTW)

Not to my knowledge.  Get 'em with darts or arrows or wands or
spells or whatever.  Or genocide 'em.

: 2) Would I have been able to recover those rings from the sink?
: (and if so, will they be waiting for me on the bones level? [RoTC is very 
: useful])

Nope, I don't think so.  Sinks have a chance when you quaff
from them to create a ring (or is it kick them?  or both?).
You can only get ore ring per sink, and I'm pretty sure that
it's randomly created.

: Somewhat unrelated:
: Someone told me once that by eating a troll corpse, you regenerate your
: hit points faster. I think there is no regeneration intrinsic, but could
: I be wrong?

Troll corpses don't help you regenerate at all.  But if you
eat a ring of regeneration you can get intrinsic regeneration.
The source refers to this as "probably stupid."  It is also
possible, by the same method, to get intrinsic hunger, but
the source just refers to this as "stupid."

And how do you eat a ring?  Become a metallovore for metal
rings or a jelly cube for wooden rings.  The only use for
jelly cubes I can think of, other than corpse eating.

